# A raised-cosine offset: the shorter the bend, the larger the radiation loss.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title S-bend shifting a 0.5 um guide by 4 um over 80 um
window width=24 length=100
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide sbend x0=0 x1=4 width=0.5 from=10 to=90
guide straight x=4 width=0.5 from=90 to=100
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=100 x=4 width=0.5
plane end z=100
expect power out 0.999815729 2e-7
expect total end 0.999986412 2e-7
expect centroid end 4.0003049 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2995921 2e-6
expect neff 2.015454774 2e-8
